kbar and select ''Sound settings''.\\n2. Under ''Input'', check that the correct microphone is selected.\\n3. Click on the microphone and ensure the volume is not at 0.\\n4. Test the microphone by speaking \\u2014 the input level indicator should move.\\n5. Under ''Output'', verify the correct speakers/headset is selected. Step 4: Run Windows Audio Troubleshooter. Windows has a built-in troubleshooter that can detect and fix common audio problems. 1. Open Windows Settings (Win + I).\\n2. Go to System > Troubleshoot > Other troubleshooters.\\n3. Find ''Recording Audio'' and click ''Run''.\\n4. Follow the on-screen instructions.\\n5. Restart the affected app after the troubleshooter completes. Step 5: Escalate to L2 Support \\u2014 Remote Desktop Session. If the user is unable to navigate Windows privacy settings or the issue persists after manual checks, escalate to a Level 2 support technician who can connect via a secure, time-limited remote desktop session to visually resolve the issue. This step is handled by the AI \\u2014 it will create a secure 30-minute remote desktop sharing link for a support technician to connect and resolve the issue visually. Escalation: Issues involving Windows OS-level privacy settings (microphone/camera permissions) and audio routing configurations require visual human intervention. The AI should identify this boundary and open an L2 support ticket with an ephemeral remote desktop sharing link for a technician to resolve the issue.\"}, {\"score\": 0.0621, \"title\": \"How to raise an invoice for a product\", \"url\": \"https://agnishpaul2002.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SELFHELP/pages/1441793\", \"text\": \"Overview This article explains the standard steps to raise an invoice for any product already configured in the system. Steps Go to Invoices > Raise Invoice. Select the product, enter quantity, and choose the correct tax code. Add any remarks if applicable, then click Submit. Confirm the invoice appears under ''My Invoices'' with status ''Submitted''.\"}]}", "note": "Live Jira ticket #KAN-4 successfully created in Atlassian project KAN with full conversation transcript."}','2026-09-23 10:32:29.193493');
