INSERT INTO "chat_messages" VALUES(196,49,'user','text','My Zoom audio is completely broken during all department meetings.','2026-09-25 04:38:16.326508');
INSERT INTO "chat_messages" VALUES(197,49,'bot','matches','{"ai_answer": "I understand you are having issues with your Zoom audio during department meetings. Based on the Zoom Application Troubleshooting Guide in our Confluence knowledge base, here are the steps I recommend to resolve the audio problems:\n\n1. Clear the Zoom Application Cache:\n   a. Close Zoom completely, including any background processes.\n   b. Navigate to %appdata%\\Zoom and %localappdata%\\Zoom, then delete the ''data'', ''logs'', ''report'', and ''dump'' folders.\n   c. Also check %temp% and remove any temporary files prefixed with ''Zoom''.\n   d. Relaunch Zoom and sign back in.\n\n2. Verify Audio and Camera Privacy Permissions:\n   a. Open Windows Settings > Privacy & Security.\n   b. Under App Permissions, select ''Microphone'' and ensure ''Let desktop apps access your microphone'' is enabled for Zoom.\n   c. Select ''Camera'' and ensure ''Let desktop apps access your camera'' is enabled for Zoom.\n   d. Relaunch Zoom.\n\n3. Check Sound Settings and Default Device:\n   a. Right-click the speaker icon in the taskbar and select ''Sound settings''.\n   b. Under ''Input'', check that the correct microphone is selected and the volume is not muted.\n   c. Under ''Output'', verify the correct speakers/headset is selected.\n\n4. Run the Windows Audio Troubleshooter:\n   a. Open Windows Settings > System > Troubleshoot > Other troubleshooters.\n   b. Find ''Recording Audio'' and click ''Run''.\n   c. Follow the on-screen instructions.\n   d. Restart the Zoom application after the troubleshooter completes.\n\nIf the audio issues persist after following these steps, the documentation recommends escalating to a Level 2 Support Engineer for a visual remote desktop inspection. The engineer can review Windows Event Viewer logs, inspect driver compatibility, or debug system-level group policies that may be causing the problem.\n\nPlease let me know if you have any other questions!\n\n\u26a1 **Automated Re