INSERT INTO "chat_messages" VALUES(306,76,'user','text','Hi, what are the different tax codes?','2026-09-25 10:16:18.282764');
INSERT INTO "chat_messages" VALUES(307,76,'bot','text','Okay, let me provide an overview of the different tax codes used in the invoicing system:

### 📋 Tax Code Overview

The tax codes determine how tax is calculated and reported for each invoice, based on the GST (Goods and Services Tax) brackets:

- **GST 5%**: Applies to select essential product categories.
- **GST 12%**: Applies to standard mid-tier products.
- **GST 18%**: The default rate for most catalog items.
- **GST 28% (New Category)**: Used for newly onboarded product categories. Invoices using this bracket require Remarks explaining the classification, for audit purposes.

If you''re unsure which tax code to use, you can:

- Check the product''s category listing
- Raise a query with the Finance Configuration team

Let me know if you have any other questions!','2026-09-25 10:16:18.282770');
