INSERT INTO "chat_messages" VALUES(322,78,'bot','text','Hello! Welcome to the Meridian Enterprise AI Helpdesk. I''m here to assist you with any issues you may be experiencing with your work applications and devices. How can I help you today? I''m knowledgeable in troubleshooting tools like Zoom, as well as providing guidance on invoices, tax codes, and remote device remediation. Please let me know what I can do for you.','2026-09-28 05:01:55.897868');
INSERT INTO "chat_messages" VALUES(323,78,'user','text','My webcam is not working','2026-09-28 05:02:54.948166');
INSERT INTO "chat_messages" VALUES(324,78,'bot','text','I apologize, but it seems the issue you are experiencing is related to your webcam not working properly. Based on the troubleshooting steps provided in the Verified Confluence Documentation, this appears to be an issue with your Windows 11 privacy settings or audio/video device configurations.

To resolve this, I would recommend the following steps:

1. Check your Windows 11 Privacy Settings for Microphone and Camera access:
   - Open the Windows Settings app (Win + I)
   - Navigate to Privacy & Security > Microphone and ensure ''Microphone access'' and ''Let apps access your microphone'' are turned on.
   - Navigate to Privacy & Security > Camera and ensure ''Camera access'' and ''Let apps access your camera'' are turned on.
   - Also check that the specific apps you are using (e.g. Teams, Zoom) have microphone and camera access enabled.

2. Verify your default audio input and output devices:
   - Right-click the speaker icon in the taskbar and select ''Sound settings''.
   - Under ''Input'', check that the correct microphone is selected and the volume is not muted.
   - Under ''Output'', verify the correct speakers/headset is selected.

3. Run the Windows Audio Troubleshooter:
   - Open the Windows Settings app (Win + I)
   - Go to System > Troubleshoot > Other troubleshooters
   - Find ''Recording Audio'' and click ''Run''
   - Follow the on-screen instructions to let the troubleshooter detect and fix any audio issues.

If you are still unable to resolve the issue after trying these steps, I would recommend escalating to a Level 2 Support Technician who can connect to your device remotely and visually inspect the problem. This will allow them to provide more advanced troubleshooting and resolve the issue.

