INSERT INTO "chat_messages" VALUES(342,82,'bot','text','Understood, let''s troubleshoot the webcam issue step-by-step:

First, let''s check your Windows privacy settings for the camera:

1. Open the Windows Settings app (Windows key + I).
2. Go to Privacy & Security > Camera.
3. Ensure the "Camera access" setting is turned on.
4. Also make sure the specific app you''re using (e.g. Zoom, Teams) has camera access enabled.

If the camera privacy settings look correct, let''s also check the default camera selection:

1. Right-click the speaker icon in the taskbar and select "Open Sound settings".
2. Under the "Input" tab, ensure the correct webcam is selected as the default recording device.
3. Check that the volume level is not muted or too low.

If the privacy settings and default device look good, the next step would be to run the Windows troubleshooter for audio/video issues:

1. Open the Windows Settings app again.
2. Go to System > Troubleshoot > Other troubleshooters.
3. Find the "Recording Audio" troubleshooter and click "Run" to diagnose any audio/video problems.

Please let me know if the webcam is still not working after trying these steps. If the issue persists, I can escalate this to our Level 2 support team who can remotely assist you through a secure desktop sharing session.','2026-09-28 05:40:00.725294');
