INSERT INTO "chat_messages" VALUES(371,88,'user','text','What are the different tax codes?','2026-09-28 06:44:07.027782');
INSERT INTO "chat_messages" VALUES(372,88,'bot','text','Based on the Confluence documentation provided, there are several tax codes used for calculating GST (Goods and Services Tax) on invoices:

- GST 5%: Applies to select essential product categories
- GST 12%: Applies to standard mid-tier products  
- GST 18%: The default rate for most catalog items
- GST 28% (New Category): Used for newly onboarded product categories. Invoices using this 28% bracket require additional remarks explaining the classification for audit purposes.

The documentation recommends checking the product''s category listing to determine the applicable GST rate. If you are unsure which tax code to use, you can raise a query with the Finance Configuration team.

The key points are:

1. Different GST percentages apply based on the product category
2. 18% is the default rate for most items
3. 28% is for new categories and requires additional remarks
4. Consult the product category listing or Finance team if unsure

Let me know if you need any clarification or have additional questions!','2026-09-28 06:44:14.064185');
