INSERT INTO "chat_messages" VALUES(385,90,'user','text','I tried these steps but the issue is still there.','2026-09-28 06:58:04.064809');
INSERT INTO "chat_messages" VALUES(386,90,'bot','text','Since adjusting the Windows camera privacy settings did not resolve the webcam issue, let''s move to the next troubleshooting step.

Many webcam problems can be caused by outdated or corrupted camera drivers. The recommended action is to update the webcam drivers to the latest version from the manufacturer.

### 📋 Recommended Action: Update Webcam Drivers

Here are the steps to update your webcam drivers:

1. Press the Windows key + X and select "Device Manager" from the menu
2. In Device Manager, expand the "Imaging devices" or "Cameras" section
3. Right-click on your webcam device name and select "Update driver"
4. Choose "Search automatically for updated driver software"
5. Windows will search online and attempt to install the latest drivers

If Windows is unable to find updated drivers automatically, you may need to manually download the latest drivers from your webcam manufacturer''s website and install them.

After updating the drivers, restart your computer and try using the webcam again in various apps. An updated driver can often resolve freezing, not detecting, or performance issues.

Please let me know if updating the webcam drivers fixes the problem or if you need any other assistance!','2026-09-28 06:58:09.852697');
