INSERT INTO "chat_messages" VALUES(417,95,'bot','text','Got it, thanks for providing those details. Based on your responses:

- The camera/webcam is not working
- You are using a laptop''s built-in webcam (not an external USB camera)
- The camera privacy indicator light is not turning on when trying to use the camera
- Your microphone is working properly

Since this seems to be an issue specific to the laptop''s webcam and not the microphone, let''s focus on resolving the camera privacy settings first.

### 📋 Recommended Action: Check Windows Camera Privacy Settings

The knowledge base article suggests that Windows 11 has built-in privacy controls that can block camera access for apps. To fix this, we need to manually adjust the settings:

1. Open the Windows 11 Settings app (press Win + I)
2. Go to Privacy & Security > Camera
3. Ensure "Camera access" is turned ON
4. Under "Allow access to the camera on this device", ensure the toggle is switched ON
5. Scroll down to "Allow apps to access your camera" and make sure this is also turned ON
6. Finally, scroll down to the list of apps and ensure the app you are trying to use (e.g. Zoom, Teams, your browser, etc.) has camera access permitted

After making these camera privacy setting changes, try using your laptop''s webcam again in the problematic application. Let me know if the camera starts working properly.

If not, we can try some additional troubleshooting steps from the knowledge base article. But adjusting these Windows camera privacy settings is the first recommended step.','2026-09-28 09:15:05.719131');
