Clearing the Zoom cache can often resolve freezing or unresponsive behavior by purging corrupted temporary files that Zoom uses. This forces Zoom to rebuild a fresh cache on the next launch.

> ⚡ **Remote Fix Available:** I can execute this Zoom cache clear remotely on your device so you don''t have to do it manually. Would you like me to proceed with the remote Zoom cache clear?','2026-09-29 08:42:15.012722');
INSERT INTO "chat_messages" VALUES(516,112,'user','text','yes','2026-09-29 08:42:34.484258');
INSERT INTO "chat_messages" VALUES(517,112,'bot','text','⚡ **Remote Action Executed**

The Zoom cache clear command has been successfully executed on your managed device (**AVDGLS5-4**).

**Actions Executed:**
• Stopped active Zoom background processes (`Zoom`, `ZoomOpener`, `CptHost`)
• Purged corrupted application caches and CEF webcache files in `AppData\Local\Zoom` and `AppData\Roaming\Zoom`
• Cleaned temporary lock files

> 💬 **Next Steps:** Please launch Zoom again and sign in.

