INSERT INTO "chat_messages" VALUES(579,128,'bot','text','Hello! I''m your Self Help Assistant. Welcome, it''s great to meet you. As your digital support companion, I''m here to help troubleshoot any issues you may have with work applications like Zoom, Microsoft Teams, or other enterprise tools. I can also assist with resolving audio, video, camera, or microphone problems, provide guidance on invoices and tax codes, and even execute remote remediation actions on your devices with your permission. How can I assist you today? Please let me know what kind of help you need, and I''ll do my very best to resolve your issue efficiently and professionally.','2026-11-10 10:53:20.523117');
INSERT INTO "chat_messages" VALUES(580,128,'user','text','how can I raise an invoice?','2026-11-10 10:53:52.577142');
INSERT INTO "chat_messages" VALUES(581,128,'bot','text','Thanks for your question on how to raise an invoice. Based on the Confluence documentation provided, here are the steps to raise an invoice for a product:

### How to Raise an Invoice

1. Go to the Invoices section and click on "Raise Invoice"
2. Select the product you want to invoice from the dropdown list
3. Enter the quantity for the product
4. Choose the correct tax code that applies
5. Add any additional remarks if needed 
6. Click "Submit" to generate the invoice

Once submitted, the invoice will appear under "My Invoices" with a status of "Submitted". It will then go through an approval workflow before being finalized.

Let me know if you need any clarification or have additional questions! I''d be happy to provide more details from the Confluence guidelines.','2026-11-10 10:54:00.135154');
INSERT INTO "chat_messages" VALUES(582,128,'user','text','Dropdown menu is not showing products','2026-11-10 12:03:19.200263');
INSERT INTO "chat_messages" VALUES(583,128,'bot','text','### 📋 Recommended Action: Add Product to Invoicing Catalog

It seems that the specific product you need is not appearing in the invoice dropdown menu. In Meridian''s invoicing system, products must first be configured and enabled in the master product catalog before they can show up in the invoice dropdown list.

Here are the steps to request adding a new product to the invoicing catalog:

1. **Identify the product details:** Make a note of the exact product name, SKU/ID, description, pricing tier and any other relevant identifiers for the product you need invoiced.

2. **Raise a Support Ticket:** Use the internal support portal to raise a ticket requesting that the product be added to the invoicing catalog master list.

3. **Provide product details:** In the support ticket, include all of the product information you gathered in step 1. This will allow the Support Engineering team to correctly configure the new product entry.

4. **Wait for confirmation:** The Support Engineers will process your request and enable the product in the catalog within 1-2 business days. You will receive a notification once completed.

5. **Verify in invoice dropdown:** After receiving the confirmation, you should be able to see the newly added product populate in the invoice dropdown menu.

Let me know if you would like me to go ahead and raise the support ticket to have this product enabled in the invoicing catalog for you.','2026-11-10 12:04:12.382921');
INSERT INTO "chat_messages" VALUES(584,128,'user','text','I verified that. The dropdown should show products','2026-11-10 12:05:58.632750');
INSERT INTO "chat_messages" VALUES(585,128,'bot','text','Got it, thanks for confirming that you have already verified the product should be available in the invoice dropdown but it is not showing up correctly.

Since we have already checked that the product is configured properly in the master catalog, this appears to be an issue with the invoicing application itself not displaying items as expected.

### 🔍 Next Steps

At this stage, I would recommend we try clearing the local cache for the invoicing application on your device. Cached data can sometimes get stuck and cause products to not display properly in the UI.

> ⚡ **Remote Cache Clear Available:** I can remotely clear the cache for the invoicing app to try resolving this product visibility issue on your device. Would you like me to go ahead and execute that remote cache clear?

If clearing the cache does not resolve the missing product dropdown issue, then the next step would be to escalate this to our Support Engineering team who can further investigate potential bugs or misconfigurations in the invoicing application backend.

Please let me know if you''d like me to proceed with the remote cache clear, or if you have any other questions!','2026-11-10 12:06:05.857351');
